-- =========================================================================
-- Mework agent kernel interaction protocol (CSP-M requirements layer).
--
-- This is the authoritative kernel interaction protocol. It defines which
-- process offers each event, in which phase, and with which synchronization.
-- The TLA+ safety layer (`formal/tla/AgentKernel.tla`) defines forbidden states;
-- this layer decomposes the same event vocabulary into processes.
--
-- Channel names must exactly match TLA+ action names and Rust
-- `KernelEvent::NAMES`. MAIN must accept exactly the traces accepted by the
-- safety model. The verifier checks vocabulary parity, exhaustive CSP-TLA
-- composition without invariant counterexamples, and trace replay in both
-- oracles. MAIN and NoAdversary must be deadlock-free.
--
-- Keep this specification small enough for line-by-line review. The CSP mutation
-- matrix must make an assertion fail when any protocol constraint is weakened.
--
-- All tasks are asynchronous. AgentSpawn is non-blocking; the model waits for
-- a task result only through task_wait. ContextEdit is offered only by TURN's
-- idle state. Persisted data is authoritative, runtime state is a cache, and
-- edited content is opaque to the kernel, so ContextEdit has no state effect.
--
-- Providers sequence turns into rounds. RoundStart dispatches one model call;
-- RoundEnd completes that call's processing. Call pipelines, AgentSpawn, and
-- TaskWait exist within a round; RoundEnd requires every call slot to settle.
-- Between rounds, the host may merge steer input and push folds.
--
-- `roundDue` is a delivery obligation. TurnStart, SteerJoin, AgentFold, and
-- in-round deliverables require a later round to deliver content to the model.
-- RoundStart consumes the obligation. A normal turn cannot end with an obligation;
-- TurnCancel abandons all obligations. AgentFold is prep-only, applies only to
-- done results, and creates `roundDue`. Done results during a running round must
-- be consumed by task_wait or delivered through AgentFold.
--
-- SteerEnqueue is available in an active turn, including cancellation. SteerJoin
-- is prep-only and creates `roundDue`. Pending steer blocks RoundStart and normal
-- TurnEnd, except cancellation preserves it for the next turn.
--
-- task_wait is a timed, result-blocking wait. TaskWait starts a wait within a
-- round. TaskWaitDeliver is offered only after the task settles; a wait for an
-- already settled task can deliver immediately. Progress updates never complete
-- a wait and are delivered only with the final result.
--
-- A multi-task task_wait completes only when every selected task delivers or its
-- timeout expires. Each task slot owns an independent pending wait; a delivery
-- returns only that slot to ANone. RoundEnd synchronizes with all task slots and
-- no waiting state offers RoundEnd.
--
-- TaskWaitTimeout withdraws an undelivered wait only when its deadline expires
-- or its own task becomes non-running without an envelope. A sibling delivery or
-- a progress update never withdraws a wait. Only running tasks may time out;
-- waits for settled tasks must deliver. Timeout receipts create `roundDue`.
--
-- A wait can target only the current task identity in its own slot. At most one
-- wait is pending per task. Pending waits block RoundEnd and are abandoned by
-- TurnCancel, after which they cannot deliver.
--
-- Synchronous tool calls carry no identity: request, authorization, execution,
-- receipt, and archival use one host-held call object within one round. The host
-- holding that object is environmental assumption A3.
--
-- Asynchronous tasks carry task identity `r`. AgentSpawn mints an identity that
-- differs from the previous generation in its slot. Completion, waiting,
-- delivery, and folding must submit the current identity; mismatches reject late
-- events from an old generation. This preserves the cross-generation portion of
-- environmental assumption A2.
--
-- The initial identity is 1, so the first task generation uses 2. Identity
-- persists across turns.
--
-- Every host-embedded model or agent loop is a task and must use a task-slot
-- pipeline. Spawn acknowledgement returns immediately; results are delivered by
-- TaskWaitDeliver or AgentFold. Such loops must not nest a model loop inside a
-- synchronous call.
--
-- A synchronous call carries a deadline, and expiry does not abandon the work.
-- ToolBackground hands the still-running host process from an executing call
-- slot to a free task slot, which mints a fresh identity exactly as AgentSpawn
-- does. The call is not cut short by the handoff: it stays in the pipeline and
-- settles normally, its receipt now naming the task instead of carrying output.
-- This is the only event that crosses the call and task surfaces, so it
-- synchronizes both slots plus the concurrency cap.
--
-- The deadline itself stays outside this clockless protocol. What is modelled is
-- the consequence: one call may hand off at most once, only while executing, and
-- only into an empty task slot within capacity. When no task slot is free the
-- host has no handoff to make and the deadline simply kills the command, which
-- is an ordinary failed receipt and needs no vocabulary of its own.
--
-- bash and powershell accept `run_in_background`. A background leg is an
-- explicitly requested asynchronous task: it uses a task-slot pipeline, consumes
-- approval before spawning, returns its spawn acknowledgement immediately, and
-- delivers results through TaskWaitDeliver or AgentFold. Stopping such a task is
-- not a separate protocol event: it produces a terminal result like any other.
-- A handed-off task is indistinguishable from an explicitly backgrounded one
-- once it is running: same completion, wait, fold, and cross-turn survival.
--
-- Tasks outlive turns. ARunning and ARunningCx offer TurnEnd and retain the
-- current identity through idle. A task completing in idle creates a wake
-- obligation: AIdleDone can exit only through TurnStart, then the result is
-- folded before the new turn's first RoundStart. Every task already done at
-- TurnStart must fold; tasks completing after TurnStart retain ordinary round
-- semantics. Cancellation may defer these results to the next TurnStart.
-- The host test suite covers wake timing.
--
-- No terminal result is ever silently discarded, and the protocol has no
-- archival path. AgentComplete is the single exit from running, whatever ended
-- the task — the model finishing, a host failure, or the user closing it from
-- the sidebar — and every such result must be taken by a wait or pushed by a
-- fold. A done task remains across cancellation and is folded in a later turn.
-- TurnCancel cancels the model turn, its pending waits, and delivery
-- obligations, but not tasks.
--
-- `awaiting_user` uses the cancellation-settlement projection. It does not
-- interrupt background tasks.
--
-- web_search and web_fetch use the call-slot pipeline, not the task surface.
-- They mint no task identity, cannot be named by task_wait, do not fold or wake,
-- and return through their own ToolRequest -> authorization -> ToolExecStart ->
-- ToolExecEnd -> ToolSettle pipeline.
--
-- The task surface consists of host-embedded model or agent loops and explicitly
-- backgrounded host work. Search and fetch are neither: a native search request
-- is a tool-free external request, not an agent loop, and neither has a model
-- background option.
--
-- Calls in a round may execute concurrently. Their slot processes synchronize
-- only on turn events, PolicyTighten, and RoundEnd, so either execution may
-- finish first. RoundEnd is available only after every call settles; results
-- from concurrently dispatched search calls are therefore delivered together in
-- the next round. A call that handed its work off still has to settle, so a
-- handoff postpones nothing about round closure.
--
-- SCEN_APPROVE and BAD_ROUNDEND_UNSETTLED_CALL cover this behavior.
--
-- Finite abstraction matching KernelConfig::MODEL_SCOPE: call slots 1..2,
-- task slots 1..2, maximum concurrency 1, and task identities {1..2}. Slots
-- are reusable containers, not globally unique IDs; `other(r)` ensures adjacent
-- generations use distinct identities.
-- =========================================================================

nametype CallSlots = {1..2}
nametype AgentSlots = {1..2}
nametype TaskIds = {1..2}

MaxLiveAgents = 1

-- Finite nonce freshness: a new task identity must differ from its predecessor.
other(r) = 3 - r

channel TurnStart, TurnCancel, TurnEnd, ContextEdit, PolicyTighten
channel RoundStart, RoundEnd, SteerEnqueue, SteerJoin
channel ToolRequest : CallSlots.Bool
channel ToolAllow, ToolApprove, ToolDeny, ToolExecStart, ToolExecEnd, ToolSettle : CallSlots
channel AgentSpawn, AgentComplete, AgentFold : AgentSlots.TaskIds
channel TaskWait, TaskWaitDeliver, TaskWaitTimeout : AgentSlots.TaskIds
channel ToolBackground : CallSlots.AgentSlots.TaskIds

-- ToolBackground is the one event both a call slot and a task slot must agree
-- on, so each side needs the projection the `{| |}` prefix notation cannot
-- express: a call slot binds the first field, a task slot the second.
ToolBackgroundFrom(c) = {| ToolBackground.c |}
ToolBackgroundInto(a) = { ToolBackground.c.a.r | c <- CallSlots, r <- TaskIds }

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Turn process: outer user-visible loop with pending steer bit `s`, retained
-- across turns. Context is editable only while idle. SteerEnqueue is available
-- during an active turn; SteerJoin clears `s` during prep. Pending steer blocks
-- a normal start or end; TCX preserves it for the next turn.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

TURN(s) = ContextEdit -> TURN(s)
       [] TurnStart -> TRUN(s)
TRUN(s) = (not s) & RoundStart -> TRUN(s)
       [] SteerEnqueue -> TRUN(true)
       [] s & SteerJoin -> TRUN(false)
       [] (not s) & TurnEnd -> TURN(s)
       [] TurnCancel -> TCX(s)
TCX(s) = SteerEnqueue -> TCX(true)
      [] TurnEnd -> TURN(s)

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Round process: WPrep is the inter-round boundary, WRound is in-round, `due`
-- is the delivery obligation, and `cx` records cancellation. Model actions are
-- in-round; SteerJoin and AgentFold are prep-only. TurnStart, SteerJoin,
-- AgentFold, and in-round deliverables create `due`; RoundStart consumes it.
-- TaskWait starts a wait but delivers no content and creates no due.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

WPrep(due, cx) = TurnStart -> WPrep(true, false)
            [] SteerJoin -> WPrep(true, cx)
            [] AgentFold?a?r -> WPrep(true, cx)
            [] due & RoundStart -> WRound(false, cx)
            [] ((not due) or cx) & TurnEnd -> WPrep(false, false)
            [] TurnCancel -> WPrep(due, true)
WRound(due, cx) = ToolRequest?c?d -> WRound(due, cx)
             [] AgentSpawn?a?r -> WRound(true, cx)
             [] ToolBackground?c?a?r -> WRound(due, cx)
             [] TaskWait?a?r -> WRound(due, cx)
             [] TaskWaitDeliver?a?r -> WRound(true, cx)
             [] TaskWaitTimeout?a?r -> WRound(true, cx)
             [] ToolSettle?c -> WRound(true, cx)
             [] RoundEnd -> WPrep(due, cx)
             [] TurnCancel -> WRound(due, true)

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Call process: one per call slot. The pipeline is request -> allow/approve/deny
-- -> execute -> receipt -> settle. `fresh` is an unconsumed authorization not
-- invalidated by PolicyTighten. Synchronous calls carry no identity because the
-- host holds the call object throughout the pipeline (assumption A3).
-- PolicyTighten synchronizes every call slot and clears `fresh`. Unsettled slots
-- do not offer RoundEnd.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- idle between turns: every call slot is empty.
CIdle(c) = TurnStart -> CUnused(c)
        [] PolicyTighten -> CIdle(c)

CUnused(c) = ToolRequest.c?d -> CRequested(c, d)
          [] RoundEnd -> CUnused(c)
          [] PolicyTighten -> CUnused(c)
          [] TurnCancel -> CUnusedCx(c)
          [] TurnEnd -> CIdle(c)

-- S1: safe calls are automatically allowed; dangerous calls require user
-- approval. Both kinds may be denied.
CRequested(c, false) = ToolAllow.c -> CAllowed(c, false, true)
                    [] ToolDeny.c -> CDenied(c)
                    [] PolicyTighten -> CRequested(c, false)
                    [] TurnCancel -> CPendingCx(c)
CRequested(c, true) = ToolApprove.c -> CAllowed(c, true, true)
                   [] ToolDeny.c -> CDenied(c)
                   [] PolicyTighten -> CRequested(c, true)
                   [] TurnCancel -> CPendingCx(c)

-- S2+S3: execution consumes `fresh`. Policy tightening clears it, requiring a
-- new authorization. Safe calls use ToolAllow and dangerous calls ToolApprove.
CAllowed(c, false, fresh) = fresh & ToolExecStart.c -> CExecuting(c)
                         [] ToolAllow.c -> CAllowed(c, false, true)
                         [] PolicyTighten -> CAllowed(c, false, false)
                         [] TurnCancel -> CPendingCx(c)
CAllowed(c, true, fresh) = fresh & ToolExecStart.c -> CExecuting(c)
                        [] ToolApprove.c -> CAllowed(c, true, true)
                        [] PolicyTighten -> CAllowed(c, true, false)
                        [] TurnCancel -> CPendingCx(c)

-- S7: only executing offers exactly one ToolExecEnd receipt. S12: an executing
-- call may hand its work to a free task slot exactly once; CExecutingBg is
-- still executing for every other purpose, which is what makes the handoff
-- unrepeatable without weakening the receipt rule.
CExecuting(c) = ToolExecEnd.c -> CDone(c)
             [] ToolBackground.c?a?r -> CExecutingBg(c)
             [] PolicyTighten -> CExecuting(c)
             [] TurnCancel -> CExecutingCx(c)
CExecutingBg(c) = ToolExecEnd.c -> CDone(c)
               [] PolicyTighten -> CExecutingBg(c)
               [] TurnCancel -> CExecutingCx(c)
CDone(c) = ToolSettle.c -> CUnused(c)
        [] PolicyTighten -> CDone(c)
        [] TurnCancel -> CSettleableCx(c)
CDenied(c) = ToolSettle.c -> CUnused(c)
          [] PolicyTighten -> CDenied(c)
          [] TurnCancel -> CSettleableCx(c)

-- Cancellation settlement (S4+S5): no new request, authorization, or execution
-- is accepted. In-flight execution may finish, and only this path discards an
-- unsettled call. Settlement completes in-round, then CUnusedCx offers RoundEnd.
CUnusedCx(c) = RoundEnd -> CUnusedCx(c)
            [] PolicyTighten -> CUnusedCx(c)
            [] TurnEnd -> CIdle(c)
CPendingCx(c) = ToolSettle.c -> CUnusedCx(c)
             [] PolicyTighten -> CPendingCx(c)
CExecutingCx(c) = ToolExecEnd.c -> CSettleableCx(c)
              [] PolicyTighten -> CExecutingCx(c)
CSettleableCx(c) = ToolSettle.c -> CUnusedCx(c)
               [] PolicyTighten -> CSettleableCx(c)

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Task process: one per task slot, retaining current or prior identity `r` across
-- turns. Spawn is non-blocking and mints `other(r)`; every subsequent task event
-- must submit that identity, rejecting late old-generation events. Completion is
-- environment-driven and may occur across rounds and turns; it is the only exit
-- from running, whatever ended the task. TaskWait starts one pending wait on a
-- running or settled task; TaskWaitDeliver is offered only for a settled task.
-- Waiting blocks RoundEnd. Without a wait, done offers prep-only AgentFold. A
-- running task survives TurnEnd. Idle completion wakes via AIdleDone and
-- TurnStart. Cancellation abandons waits and turn actions but lets tasks cross
-- TurnEnd, retaining done results for later fold.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

AIdle(a, r) = TurnStart -> ANone(a, r)
           [] RoundStart -> AIdle(a, r)
ANone(a, r) = AgentSpawn.a!other(r) -> ARunning(a, other(r))
           [] ToolBackground?c!a!other(r) -> ARunning(a, other(r))
           [] RoundEnd -> ANone(a, r)
           [] TurnCancel -> ANoneCx(a, r)
           [] TurnEnd -> AIdle(a, r)
           [] RoundStart -> ANone(a, r)
ARunning(a, r) = AgentComplete.a.r -> ADone(a, r)
              [] TaskWait.a.r -> AWaitRunning(a, r)
              [] RoundEnd -> ARunning(a, r)
              [] TurnCancel -> ARunningCx(a, r)
              [] TurnEnd -> AIdleRunning(a, r)
              [] RoundStart -> ARunning(a, r)
ADone(a, r) = TaskWait.a.r -> AWaitDone(a, r)
           [] AgentFold.a.r -> ANone(a, r)
           [] RoundEnd -> ADone(a, r)
           [] TurnCancel -> ADoneCx(a, r)
           [] RoundStart -> ADone(a, r)

-- Waiting states do not offer RoundEnd. A waiting task may settle; a running
-- wait may time out, while a settled wait must deliver. TurnCancel abandons the
-- wait: done is retained and running continues.
AWaitRunning(a, r) = AgentComplete.a.r -> AWaitDone(a, r)
                  [] TaskWaitTimeout.a.r -> ARunning(a, r)
                  [] TurnCancel -> ARunningCx(a, r)
                  [] RoundStart -> AWaitRunning(a, r)
AWaitDone(a, r) = TaskWaitDeliver.a.r -> ANone(a, r)
              [] TurnCancel -> ADoneCx(a, r)
              [] RoundStart -> AWaitDone(a, r)

-- Cancellation settlement (S4+S11) accepts no new wait, delivery, or fold.
-- Tasks cross TurnEnd and done is retained for the next turn.
ANoneCx(a, r) = RoundEnd -> ANoneCx(a, r)
             [] TurnEnd -> AIdle(a, r)
             [] RoundStart -> ANoneCx(a, r)
ARunningCx(a, r) = AgentComplete.a.r -> ADoneCx(a, r)
                [] RoundEnd -> ARunningCx(a, r)
                [] TurnEnd -> AIdleRunning(a, r)
                [] RoundStart -> ARunningCx(a, r)
ADoneCx(a, r) = RoundEnd -> ADoneCx(a, r)
            [] TurnEnd -> AIdleDone(a, r)
            [] RoundStart -> ADoneCx(a, r)

-- S11: only tasks already done when TurnStart occurs block the first round.
-- Other states offer RoundStart without imposing another window/turn guard;
-- TURN and ROUND retain those independent obligations and their mutation probes.
AIdleRunning(a, r) = AgentComplete.a.r -> AIdleDone(a, r)
                  [] TurnStart -> ARunning(a, r)
                  [] RoundStart -> AIdleRunning(a, r)
AIdleDone(a, r) = TurnStart -> AWakeDone(a, r)
               [] RoundStart -> AIdleDone(a, r)
AWakeDone(a, r) = AgentFold.a.r -> ANone(a, r)
               [] TurnCancel -> ADoneCx(a, r)

-- S6: the concurrency limit is a cross-slot constraint enforced by synchronizing
-- the capacity process with every task slot. The running count decrements on
-- Complete, the sole exit from running; composition keeps `n` non-negative.
-- A handed-off call occupies a task slot exactly like a spawn, so it is counted
-- by the same cap rather than a second one.
CAPACITY(n) = (n < MaxLiveAgents) & AgentSpawn?a?r -> CAPACITY(n + 1)
           [] (n < MaxLiveAgents) & ToolBackground?c?a?r -> CAPACITY(n + 1)
           [] AgentComplete?a?r -> CAPACITY(n - 1)

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Composition. Turn events synchronize all processes. TurnEnd requires call
-- slots to be settled; tasks may remain running, but done results must be folded
-- or delivered, except done results retained across cancellation. ROUND controls
-- window events. RoundEnd requires settled calls and no pending task wait.
-- PolicyTighten synchronizes all call slots; spawn and completion synchronize
-- matching task slots and capacity. ContextEdit belongs only to TURN.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

TurnEvents = {TurnStart, TurnCancel, TurnEnd}
TurnAlpha = union(TurnEvents, {ContextEdit, SteerEnqueue, SteerJoin, RoundStart})
RoundAlpha = union(union(TurnEvents, {RoundStart, RoundEnd, SteerJoin}),
                   union({| ToolRequest, ToolSettle, AgentSpawn, TaskWait, TaskWaitDeliver,
                            TaskWaitTimeout, AgentFold |},
                         {| ToolBackground |}))
CallAlpha(c) = union(TurnEvents,
                     union(union({PolicyTighten, RoundEnd},
                                 {| ToolRequest.c, ToolAllow.c, ToolApprove.c, ToolDeny.c,
                                    ToolExecStart.c, ToolExecEnd.c, ToolSettle.c |}),
                           ToolBackgroundFrom(c)))
AgentAlpha(a) = union(TurnEvents,
                      union(union({RoundStart, RoundEnd},
                                  {| AgentSpawn.a, AgentComplete.a, AgentFold.a,
                                     TaskWait.a, TaskWaitDeliver.a, TaskWaitTimeout.a |}),
                            ToolBackgroundInto(a)))
CapAlpha = union({| AgentSpawn, AgentComplete |}, {| ToolBackground |})
CallsAlpha = union(CallAlpha(1), CallAlpha(2))
AgentsAlpha = union(AgentAlpha(1), AgentAlpha(2))
SlotsAlpha = union(CallsAlpha, union(AgentsAlpha, CapAlpha))

CALLS = CIdle(1) [ CallAlpha(1) || CallAlpha(2) ] CIdle(2)
AGENTS = AIdle(1, 1) [ AgentAlpha(1) || AgentAlpha(2) ] AIdle(2, 1)
AGENTS_CAPPED = AGENTS [ AgentsAlpha || CapAlpha ] CAPACITY(0)
SLOTS = CALLS [ CallsAlpha || union(AgentsAlpha, CapAlpha) ] AGENTS_CAPPED
GATED = WPrep(false, false) [ RoundAlpha || SlotsAlpha ] SLOTS

MAIN = TURN(false) [ TurnAlpha || union(RoundAlpha, SlotsAlpha) ] GATED

-- Progress check: disabling PolicyTighten and SteerEnqueue must still leave the
-- protocol deadlock-free.
NoAdversary = MAIN [| {PolicyTighten, SteerEnqueue} |] STOP

-- =========================================================================
-- Scenario processes. The verifier checks positive traces with `SCEN_*` and
-- negative traces with `BAD_*`; each negative trace must be reversed by a CSP
-- mutation that weakens its constraint. First-generation task identity is 2,
-- followed by 1 and alternating thereafter.
-- =========================================================================

-- S1/S2/S7/S9: full dangerous-call approval, execution, receipt, and archival;
-- the final round delivers the receipt.
SCEN_APPROVE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolApprove.1
            -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> ToolSettle.1 -> RoundEnd
            -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S3: re-approval after policy tightening may proceed.
SCEN_REAPPROVE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolApprove.1
              -> PolicyTighten -> ToolApprove.1 -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolExecEnd.1
              -> ToolSettle.1 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S4/S5: cancellation settlement finishes in-flight execution, discards unsettled
-- calls, and closes the round while abandoning delivery obligations. A task
-- settling during cancellation is retained through ADoneCx for a later fold.
SCEN_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
           -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolRequest.2.true -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
           -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> ToolSettle.1 -> ToolSettle.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
           -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S8'/S9: context editing between turns; asynchronous spawn does not block
-- further calls, while waiting for a running task blocks until in-round delivery.
SCEN_ASYNC_WAIT = ContextEdit -> TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2
               -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1 -> ToolExecStart.1
               -> TaskWait.1.2 -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> AgentComplete.1.2
               -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> ToolSettle.1 -> RoundEnd
               -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> ContextEdit -> STOP
-- S8': a wait for an already settled task delivers immediately.
SCEN_WAIT_SETTLED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                 -> TaskWait.1.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                 -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S8': timeout withdraws a wait while the task continues; the timeout receipt is
-- delivered in the next round, and the still-running task survives the turn.
SCEN_WAIT_TIMEOUT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                 -> TaskWaitTimeout.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd
                 -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: an unclaimed done result folds in prep and triggers the next round; another
-- task's result may instead be observed by an in-round wait.
SCEN_FOLD = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2
         -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.2.2 -> AgentComplete.2.2
         -> TaskWait.2.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.2.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd
         -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: steer is enqueued in-round, joined in prep, consumed by the next round,
-- then the turn ends normally.
SCEN_STEER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> SteerEnqueue -> RoundEnd -> SteerJoin
          -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: cancellation retains pending steer for joining before the next turn's
-- first round.
SCEN_STEER_CARRYOVER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> SteerEnqueue -> TurnCancel
                    -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart -> SteerJoin -> RoundStart
                    -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: a task the user stopped mid-turn still produces a terminal result, so its
-- fold charges `roundDue` and the turn cannot end without another round.
SCEN_STOP_RETRIGGERS = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                    -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> AgentFold.1.2
                    -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S10': reusing a slot rotates task identity; each generation proceeds with its
-- current identity.
SCEN_TID_ROTATE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
               -> TaskWait.1.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> AgentSpawn.1.1
               -> AgentComplete.1.1 -> TaskWait.1.1 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.1 -> RoundEnd
               -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S11: a running task survives normal end. Idle completion wakes a new turn;
-- prep folds the result and the first round delivers it.
SCEN_TASK_SURVIVES_END = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                      -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2
                      -> TurnStart -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd
                      -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S11: the next user turn adopts a surviving task and may wait for its delivery.
SCEN_ADOPT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
          -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart -> RoundStart -> TaskWait.1.2
          -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
          -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S11: cancellation does not interrupt a task; a running task survives it and
-- idle completion still wakes a turn.
SCEN_CANCEL_RUNNING_SURVIVES = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
                            -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> TurnStart
                            -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S11: cancellation retains an already done result for folding in the next turn.
SCEN_CANCEL_DONE_CARRYOVER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                          -> TurnCancel -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart
                          -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S11: a task completing between TurnCancel and TurnEnd is also retained through
-- ADoneCx and folded in the next turn.
SCEN_CANCEL_WINDOW_COMPLETE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
                           -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart
                           -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- The cap is one live task, not one retained result: completing the first
-- before spawning the second leaves two done results to inherit on wake.
WakeTwo(next) = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
              -> AgentSpawn.2.2 -> AgentComplete.2.2 -> TurnCancel -> RoundEnd
              -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart -> next
SCEN_WAKE_TWO_FOLDS = WakeTwo(AgentFold.2.2 -> AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart
                            -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP)
SCEN_WAKE_CANCEL_RETRY = WakeTwo(AgentFold.1.2 -> TurnCancel -> TurnEnd
                               -> TurnStart -> AgentFold.2.2 -> RoundStart
                               -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP)
-- Completion after TurnStart is not an inherited result and imposes no new
-- pre-first-round obligation. It may be waited on in that first round.
SCEN_WAKE_LATE_COMPLETE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                        -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> TurnStart
                        -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> RoundStart -> TaskWait.1.2
                        -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
                        -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_WAKE_FIRST_ROUND = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                     -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2
                     -> TurnStart -> RoundStart -> STOP
BAD_WAKE_PARTIAL_FOLD = WakeTwo(AgentFold.1.2 -> RoundStart -> STOP)
BAD_WAKE_CANCEL_RETRY = WakeTwo(AgentFold.1.2 -> TurnCancel -> TurnEnd
                              -> TurnStart -> RoundStart -> STOP)
BAD_WAKE_STALE_FOLD = WakeTwo(AgentFold.1.1 -> STOP)

-- S12: an executing call whose deadline expires hands its work to a free task
-- slot and then settles normally in the same round. The task it left behind is
-- an ordinary one: it completes later and folds in prep like any other.
SCEN_BG_TIMEOUT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
               -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolBackground.1.1.2 -> ToolExecEnd.1
               -> ToolSettle.1 -> RoundEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> AgentFold.1.2
               -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S12: the handed-off task is addressable the moment the call settles, so the
-- same round may wait on it and take its result in-round.
SCEN_BG_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
            -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolBackground.1.1.2 -> ToolExecEnd.1
            -> ToolSettle.1 -> TaskWait.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
            -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd
            -> TurnEnd -> STOP

-- S1: no execution without approval; dangerous calls cannot auto-allow, and safe
-- calls cannot use user approval.
BAD_EXEC_UNAPPROVED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolExecStart.1 -> STOP
BAD_ALLOW_DANGER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolAllow.1 -> STOP
BAD_APPROVE_SAFE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolApprove.1 -> STOP
-- S3: a stale approval cannot execute after tightening. Both authorization
-- pipelines independently enforce the `fresh` guard.
BAD_STALE_EXEC = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolApprove.1
              -> PolicyTighten -> ToolExecStart.1 -> STOP
BAD_STALE_EXEC_SAFE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                   -> PolicyTighten -> ToolExecStart.1 -> STOP
-- S2: one approval cannot start execution twice.
BAD_DOUBLE_EXEC = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
               -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> ToolExecStart.1 -> STOP
-- S4: cancellation accepts no new request, spawn, wait, or round.
BAD_REQUEST_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> TurnCancel -> ToolRequest.1.false -> STOP
BAD_SPAWN_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> TurnCancel -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_WAIT_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                     -> TurnCancel -> TaskWait.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_WAIT_AFTER_CANCEL_RUNNING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
                             -> TaskWait.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_FOLD_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                     -> TurnCancel -> RoundEnd -> AgentFold.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_ROUNDSTART_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
                           -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> STOP
-- S5/S11: a normal turn cannot end with an unclaimed done result, although a
-- running task survives. Turns cannot end in-round, and unsettled calls block
-- RoundEnd.
BAD_END_PENDING_DONE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                    -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_END_INROUND = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_ROUNDEND_UNSETTLED_CALL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> RoundEnd -> STOP
-- S5: a running round cannot discard an unsettled call.
BAD_DROP_PENDING_RUNNING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolSettle.1 -> STOP
-- S8: context is frozen during an active turn, including cancellation settlement.
BAD_EDIT_RUNNING = TurnStart -> ContextEdit -> STOP
BAD_EDIT_CANCELLING = TurnStart -> TurnCancel -> ContextEdit -> STOP
-- S6: concurrency limit.
BAD_OVERCAP = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentSpawn.2.2 -> STOP
-- S7: no receipt may appear without execution.
BAD_RECEIPT_NO_EXEC = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                   -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> STOP
-- S9 delivery obligations: a user message, fold, join, or receipt must be
-- delivered by a round before normal turn end; rounds do not start without `due`.
BAD_END_NO_ROUND = TurnStart -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_IDLE_ROUND = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> STOP
BAD_END_AFTER_FOLD = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
                  -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> AgentFold.1.2 -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_END_AFTER_JOIN = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> SteerEnqueue -> RoundEnd -> SteerJoin
                  -> TurnEnd -> STOP
BAD_END_UNDELIVERED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                   -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> ToolSettle.1 -> RoundEnd
                   -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: steer is enqueued only in an active turn and joined only in prep. Pending
-- steer blocks a normal round start and turn end.
BAD_STEER_IDLE = SteerEnqueue -> STOP
BAD_STEER_JOIN_INROUND = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> SteerEnqueue -> SteerJoin -> STOP
-- S9: SteerJoin requires pending steer; TURN's `s` bit is the sole authority.
BAD_STEER_JOIN_NO_PENDING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> SteerJoin -> STOP
BAD_ROUNDSTART_PENDING_STEER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> SteerEnqueue
                            -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart -> STOP
BAD_END_PENDING_STEER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> SteerEnqueue -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- S9: AgentFold is prep-only and done-only. A running task does not fold; done
-- results cannot be silently discarded in-round, and model actions are not
-- offered during prep.
BAD_FOLD_RUNNING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                -> AgentFold.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_FOLD_INROUND = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                -> AgentFold.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_WAIT_IN_PREP = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                -> RoundEnd -> TaskWait.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_REQUEST_IN_PREP = TurnStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> STOP
BAD_SPAWN_IN_PREP = TurnStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> STOP
-- S8' waiting: empty slots cannot wait; one task has at most one pending wait.
-- Delivery requires both a settled task and a started wait. Pending waits block
-- RoundEnd, and cancellation prevents delivery.
BAD_WAIT_NO_TASK = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> TaskWait.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_DOUBLE_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
               -> TaskWait.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_DELIVER_UNSETTLED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                     -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_DELIVER_NO_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                   -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_ROUNDEND_PENDING_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                         -> RoundEnd -> STOP
BAD_ROUNDEND_PENDING_WAIT_SETTLED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2
                                 -> TaskWait.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> STOP
BAD_DELIVER_AFTER_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                        -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> TurnCancel -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> STOP
-- S8': timeout withdraws only an undelivered started wait. A settled wait must
-- deliver rather than time out, and a timeout receipt requires a delivery round.
BAD_TIMEOUT_NO_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWaitTimeout.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_TIMEOUT_SETTLED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                   -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> TaskWaitTimeout.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_END_AFTER_TIMEOUT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
                     -> TaskWait.1.2 -> TaskWaitTimeout.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> STOP
-- Cross-phase overwrite and duplicate triggers: an unsettled slot accepts no
-- request; authorization cannot affect executing or settled phases; only an
-- empty task slot can spawn; and a settled task cannot complete again.
BAD_REQUEST_OVERWRITE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false
                     -> ToolRequest.1.false -> STOP
BAD_ALLOW_EXECUTING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                   -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolAllow.1 -> STOP
BAD_APPROVE_EXECUTING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.true -> ToolApprove.1
                     -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolApprove.1 -> STOP
BAD_DENY_ALLOWED = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                -> ToolDeny.1 -> STOP
BAD_SPAWN_OVERWRITE_DONE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                        -> AgentSpawn.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_DOUBLE_COMPLETE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                   -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> STOP
-- S10': task-pipeline events must submit the current task identity. Completion,
-- waiting, delivery, and folding reject old or foreign identities, including in
-- waiting and cancellation paths.
BAD_TID_SPAWN_REPEAT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                    -> TaskWait.1.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.2 -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_TID_COMPLETE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_WAIT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_TIMEOUT = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
               -> TaskWaitTimeout.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_WAIT_DONE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                 -> TaskWait.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_COMPLETE_WAITING = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
                        -> AgentComplete.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_DELIVER = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TaskWait.1.2
               -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> TaskWaitDeliver.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_FOLD = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2
            -> AgentFold.1.1 -> STOP
BAD_TID_COMPLETE_CANCEL = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> TurnCancel
                       -> AgentComplete.1.1 -> STOP

-- S11: an idle done result cannot be folded outside prep.
BAD_FOLD_IDLE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd -> RoundStart
             -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> AgentComplete.1.2 -> AgentFold.1.2 -> STOP
-- S10' x S11: every idle-survival binding point also checks task identity.
BAD_TID_COMPLETE_IDLE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> RoundEnd
                     -> RoundStart -> RoundEnd -> TurnEnd -> AgentComplete.1.1 -> STOP

-- S12: only an executing call may hand its work off, and only once. Each of
-- these has exactly one blocking process, so a single mutation reverses it.
BAD_BG_BEFORE_EXEC = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                  -> ToolBackground.1.1.2 -> STOP
BAD_BG_AFTER_END = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
                -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolExecEnd.1 -> ToolBackground.1.1.2 -> STOP
-- The task the first handoff created is completed first, so capacity is free
-- again and the executing call slot is the only thing left refusing.
BAD_BG_TWICE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
            -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolBackground.1.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
            -> ToolBackground.1.2.2 -> STOP
-- S12 x S10': a handoff mints the same fresh identity a spawn would.
BAD_BG_STALE_ID = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1
               -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolBackground.1.1.1 -> STOP
-- S12 x S9: a slot still holding an unclaimed result is not free to receive one.
BAD_BG_SLOT_DONE = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> AgentComplete.1.2
                -> ToolRequest.1.false -> ToolAllow.1 -> ToolExecStart.1
                -> ToolBackground.1.1.1 -> STOP
-- S12 x S6: a handoff is counted by the same concurrency cap as a spawn.
BAD_BG_OVERCAP = TurnStart -> RoundStart -> AgentSpawn.1.2 -> ToolRequest.1.false
              -> ToolAllow.1 -> ToolExecStart.1 -> ToolBackground.1.2.2 -> STOP
